The '''Glacite Tunnels''' are a [[Location]] focused on {{Skill|Mining}} that requires [[Heart of the Mountain|Heart of the Mountain VII]] to be accessed. It has several unique minerals, including {{Item|Glacite}}, {{Item|Umber}}, and {{Item|Tungsten}}.  

== Accessing ==
In order to access the {{Zone|Dwarven Base Camp}} and then the '''Glacite Tunnels''', the player must forge a {{Item|Secret Railroad Pass}} after talking to {{NPCSprite|Dulin}}. The player have {{Coll|Heart of the Mountain|7}} in order to forge a {{Item|Secret Railroad Pass}}, forged with {{Item|Flawless Ruby Gemstone|amount=1}}, {{Item|Refined Mithril|amount=2}}, and {{Item|Corleonite|amount=8}} for {{Green|30}} seconds.

== Purpose ==
The Glacite Tunnels has the biggest potential for money-making for miners. In the '''Glacite Tunnels''', the player can mine [[Dwarven Metals]] like {{Item|Umber}}, {{Item|Tungsten}} and {{Item|Glacite}}. The '''Glacite Tunnels''' also contain [[Gemstone|Gemstones]], exclusive to this area, such as {{Item|Onyx Gemstone|text=Onyx}}, {{Item|Aquamarine Gemstone|text=Aquamarine}}, {{Item|Citrine Gemstone|text=Citrine}} and {{Item|Peridot Gemstone|text=Peridot}}. Inside the Tunnels, you accumulate {{Stat|Cold}}, which reduces your {{Stat|Mining Speed}} by {{red|0.5%}} per {{Stat|Cold}}. Additionally, the player's {{Stat|Speed}} is decreased by {{red|25%}} for every {{Stat|Cold|25}}. Upon reaching {{Stat|Cold|100}}, the player freezes to death and is returned to the {{Zone|Dwarven Base Camp}}.

=== Mineshafts ===
{{Main|Glacite Mineshaft}}
'''Glacite Mineshafts''' can be found by mining blocks within the {{zone|Glacite Tunnels}}. The base chance of spawning a '''Glacite Mineshaft''' is {{Green|0.05%}}, or {{Green|1 in 2,000}}. A pity system was implemented in [[Changelog/2024/April 24|Version 0.20.1]] to provide a more consistent spawn rate for '''Glacite Mineshafts'''. Each pity counter begins at {{Green|2,000}} and decreases by the numbers below for each block type. Once a '''Glacite Mineshaft''' has spawned, the counter is reset to {{Green|2,000}}.
